# Harness changes require review (design spec 11.0 "Recorded-answer integrity",
# decision H33): the oracle harness - its comparison logic, the drivers, the
# recorded answers and their hashes (golden/MANIFEST), the known divergences, the
# gate's policy and the corpus - is owned here, so a pull request that touches any
# of it asks for its owner's review. So is .github/: the workflows decide which
# tier CI runs, with which restrictions, and whether `verify` runs at all - a
# weaker invocation would make CI green without touching the harness - and this
# file says who reviews; a pull request runs its own edited workflow, and GitHub
# applies the base branch's CODEOWNERS, so both must be owned.
#
# This binds only once branch protection on `main` requires a review from a code
# owner ("Require review from Code Owners"); until then it only requests one.
/oracles/ @Silicon-Spider
/.github/ @Silicon-Spider
